WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:03.164
Factory overtime lives
in spreadsheets and chat.

00:03.164 --> 00:06.442
Hours get missed, and
payroll fixes them by hand.

00:07.800 --> 00:09.567
Overtime serves three people.

00:09.567 --> 00:13.528
Asha on the line, Vikram her
manager, Priya in payroll.

00:14.800 --> 00:16.930
One plain policy sets the rules.

00:16.930 --> 00:19.991
Five hours twenty clocked
becomes four paid hours.

00:21.800 --> 00:24.899
Asha never types hours.
Short days are blocked.

00:24.899 --> 00:28.065
She ticks two days, and
the cap meter updates.

00:29.800 --> 00:33.396
She adds a note and submits.
Both requests go to Vikram.

00:35.800 --> 00:39.710
She can withdraw until it's
decided. Now, over to Vikram.

00:40.800 --> 00:44.039
Hours arrive policy-checked,
with the amount and reason.

00:44.039 --> 00:45.879
Vikram approves in one click.

00:47.800 --> 00:49.109
Then on to payroll.

00:51.300 --> 00:53.002
Priya picks the payroll month.

00:53.002 --> 00:55.755
September hours become
an arrear on their own.

00:59.300 --> 01:04.803
The register shows regular lines, the arrear,
and a reversal for hours cut after payout.

01:07.300 --> 01:10.763
Many workers never log in,
so Vikram applies for them.

01:12.300 --> 01:16.714
Joseph's last day would cross his monthly
cap, so that row is pink and locked.

01:16.714 --> 01:18.620
The rest are approved at once.

01:21.800 --> 01:25.828
Every rupee is checked, approved
once, and paid in the right month.

01:25.828 --> 01:29.725
I took it from zero to one,
to over a hundred enterprises.

01:32.300 --> 01:35.233
Extra time in attendance, paid by the rules.
